      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;beginner-basics--fundamentals&#34;&gt;Beginner (Basics &amp;amp; Fundamentals)&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#1-what-is-git-hub&#34;&gt;What is git hub?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#2-explain-git&#34;&gt;Explain git?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#3-explain-git&#34;&gt;Explain Git?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#4-what-is-the-purpose-of-git&#34;&gt;What is the purpose of Git?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#5-why-is-git-used&#34;&gt;Why is GIT used?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#6-what-are-the-advantages-of-git-hub&#34;&gt;What are the advantages of Git Hub?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#7-why-is-github-considered-version-control&#34;&gt;Why is GitHub considered version control?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#8-currently-do-you-use-github&#34;&gt;Currently, do you use GitHub?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#9-tell-me-about-git-usage-in-your-current-project&#34;&gt;Tell me about git usage in your current project?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#10-what-are-pull-and-push&#34;&gt;What are pull and push?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#11-what-is-the-difference-between-commit-and-push-in-github&#34;&gt;What is the difference between Commit and Push in Github?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#12-explain-git-commands-commit-and-merge&#34;&gt;Explain git commands: commit and merge?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#13-what-is-the-command-to-push-code-and-to-create-a-branch&#34;&gt;What is the command to push code and to create a branch?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#14-how-do-you-create-a-branch-in-github&#34;&gt;How do you create a branch in GitHub?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#15-what-is-the-difference-between-clone-and-checkout-in-github&#34;&gt;What is the difference between clone and checkout in GitHub?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;questions-with-answers&#34;&gt;Questions with Answers&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;what-is-git-hub&#34;&gt;What is git hub?&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Answer&lt;/strong&gt;: GitHub is a cloud-based hosting service that lets you manage and share your Git repositories. It provides a web interface for collaboration and version control.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
